# Security

- Send a channel secret only after an operator approves that node.
- Resolve a 6-byte prefix to exactly one 32-byte key before a reply or a command.
- Mesh text is plain text. Never pass it to a shell, HTML, or an unconfigured URL.
- Rate-limit automatic replies. Operator sends are queued and logged in the audit table.
- The message list shows `[secret sent]`, never the secret. Do not write secrets into git or ordinary logs.
- Denying a pending node does not reveal a secret. Removing an enrolled node rotates the secret and re-sends it only to nodes that remain enrolled.
- `signup` from a denied node may return them to pending. They still need approval.
